cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Chicago / Grant Park Aerial Photogrammetry and Terrestrial Laser Dataset"
abstract: >-
  2,751 full-resolution geotagged aerial photographs (41.9 GB) and 241 terrestrial laser scan
  files across 43 stations (8.66 GB) covering Grant Park and the surrounding downtown Chicago
  blocks, captured 27-28 June 2020 with a DJI Mavic 2 Pro (Hasselblad L1D-20c) and a FARO Focus
  S150. The aerial imagery is registered to the laser point cloud, which is the scale reference
  -- GPS was not used for scale. Capture density is deliberately uneven: the wider city is
  aerial photogrammetry, while the Lollapalooza festival field, empty that summer after the
  event was cancelled, was laser scanned as the primary subject. Released as unmodified source
  capture with EXIF and GPS intact, organised by flight.
